      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Yeh Unit 5 (Partial Fractions) ke poore unit se practice long questions (tafseeli sawal) hain, Board ke Section-II ke sawal ke hisse ki shakal mein: har sawal 5 number ka hai (lamba sawal, saboot (proof) ya derivation). Har sawal poore qadmon ke saath hal kiya gaya hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "1 By long division, express \\(\\dfrac{2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - x + 4}{x^{2} + 1}\\) as the sum of a polynomial and a proper rational fraction. Check your answer at \\(x = 1\\). (5 marks)\n(Lambi taqseem se \\(\\dfrac{2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - x + 4}{x^{2} + 1}\\) ko polynomial aur proper rational fraction ke jama mein likhein. \\(x = 1\\) par jawab check karein.)",
            "explanation": "Fraction improper hai (3 > 2); itni taqseem karein ke baqi ki degree 2 se kam ho jaye.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "3d9823eb-a731-5085-ab4e-f4ec9307b4c0",
              "quote": "How the long division works, row by row"
            },
            "steps": [
              "Khaali jagah bhar kar divisor: \\(x^{2} + 0x + 1\\)",
              "\\(2x^{3} \\div x^{2} = 2x\\); \\(2x(x^{2} + 1) = 2x^{3} + 2x\\)",
              "Tafreeq: \\((2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - x + 4) - (2x^{3} + 2x) = 3x^{2} - 3x + 4\\)",
              "\\(3x^{2} \\div x^{2} = 3\\); \\(3(x^{2} + 1) = 3x^{2} + 3\\)",
              "Tafreeq: \\((3x^{2} - 3x + 4) - (3x^{2} + 3) = -3x + 1\\); degree \\(1 < 2\\), is liye ruk jayein",
              "Quotient \\(2x + 3\\), baqi \\(1 - 3x\\)",
              "\\(x = 1\\) par check: bayan \\(\\frac{2 + 3 - 1 + 4}{2} = 4\\); dayan \\(2 + 3 + \\frac{1 - 3}{2} = 4\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - x + 4}{x^{2} + 1} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac{1 - 3x}{x^{2} + 1}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "2 If \\((p + q)x^{3} + (p - q)x^{2} + (2r - p)x + s = 4x^{3} + 2x^{2} - x + 7\\) for all values of \\(x\\), find \\(p, q, r, s\\). Verify the result at \\(x = 1\\). (5 marks)\n(Agar \\(x\\) ki har qeemat par \\((p + q)x^{3} + (p - q)x^{2} + (2r - p)x + s = 4x^{3} + 2x^{2} - x + 7\\) ho to \\(p, q, r, s\\) maloom karein. \\(x = 1\\) par natija check karein.)",
            "explanation": "Dono polynomials har x par barabar hain, is liye aik jaisi powers ke coefficients barabar hain.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "3d9823eb-a731-5085-ab4e-f4ec9307b4c0",
              "quote": "The evaluation of the coefficients of the partial fractions is based on the following theorem"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(x^{3}\\): \\(p + q = 4\\) ... (1)",
              "\\(x^{2}\\): \\(p - q = 2\\) ... (2)",
              "(1) + (2): \\(2p = 6 \\Rightarrow p = 3\\); phir \\(q = 1\\)",
              "\\(x\\): \\(2r - p = -1 \\Rightarrow 2r = 2 \\Rightarrow r = 1\\)",
              "constant: \\(s = 7\\)",
              "\\(x = 1\\) par check: bayan \\(4 + 2 + (2 - 3) + 7 = 12\\); dayan \\(4 + 2 - 1 + 7 = 12\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(p = 3\\), \\(q = 1\\), \\(r = 1\\), \\(s = 7\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "3 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 2x - 5}{(x - 1)(x + 1)(x - 2)}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 2x - 5}{(x - 1)(x + 1)(x - 2)}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper fraction (2 < 3), teen mukhtalif linear factors: Case I.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "at \\(x = 2\\) the \\(A\\) and \\(C\\) terms contain the factor"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 2x - 5}{(x - 1)(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\dfrac{A}{x - 1} + \\dfrac{B}{x + 1} + \\dfrac{C}{x - 2}\\)",
              "\\(x^{2} + 2x - 5 = A(x + 1)(x - 2) + B(x - 1)(x - 2) + C(x - 1)(x + 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = 1\\): \\(1 + 2 - 5 = A(2)(-1) \\Rightarrow -2 = -2A \\Rightarrow A = 1\\)",
              "\\(x = -1\\): \\(1 - 2 - 5 = B(-2)(-3) \\Rightarrow -6 = 6B \\Rightarrow B = -1\\)",
              "\\(x = 2\\): \\(4 + 4 - 5 = C(1)(3) \\Rightarrow 3 = 3C \\Rightarrow C = 1\\)",
              "Check, \\(x^{2}\\) ka coefficient: \\(A + B + C = 1 - 1 + 1 = 1\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 2x - 5}{(x - 1)(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\dfrac{1}{x - 1} - \\dfrac{1}{x + 1} + \\dfrac{1}{x - 2}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "4 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{4x + 5}{x^{2} + x - 2}\\) into partial fractions by equating coefficients, and check by putting \\(x = 0\\). (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{4x + 5}{x^{2} + x - 2}\\) ko coefficients barabar kar ke partial fractions mein todein, aur \\(x = 0\\) rakh kar check karein.)",
            "explanation": "Denominator ke factors banayein, denominators khatam karein, phailayein aur coefficients barabar karein.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "Equate the coefficients of like terms (powers of"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(x^{2} + x - 2 = (x + 2)(x - 1)\\)",
              "\\(\\dfrac{4x + 5}{(x + 2)(x - 1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x + 2} + \\dfrac{B}{x - 1} \\Rightarrow 4x + 5 = A(x - 1) + B(x + 2)\\)",
              "\\(4x + 5 = (A + B)x + (-A + 2B)\\)",
              "\\(x\\): \\(A + B = 4\\) ... (1); constant: \\(-A + 2B = 5\\) ... (2)",
              "(1) + (2): \\(3B = 9 \\Rightarrow B = 3\\); phir \\(A = 1\\)",
              "\\(x = 0\\) par check: bayan \\(\\frac{5}{-2} = -\\frac{5}{2}\\); dayan \\(\\frac{1}{2} - 3 = -\\frac{5}{2}\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{4x + 5}{x^{2} + x - 2} = \\dfrac{1}{x + 2} + \\dfrac{3}{x - 1}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "5 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 4x + 1}{(x - 1)(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\) into partial fractions and verify the answer at \\(x = 0\\). (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 4x + 1}{(x - 1)(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein aur \\(x = 0\\) par jawab check karein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper fraction (2 < 3), Case I; factors ke zero aik aik kar ke rakhein.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "Why: at \\(x = 3\\) only the \\(C\\) term survives."
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(x^{2} + 4x + 1 = A(x + 1)(x + 2) + B(x - 1)(x + 2) + C(x - 1)(x + 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = 1\\): \\(6 = A(2)(3) \\Rightarrow A = 1\\)",
              "\\(x = -1\\): \\(1 - 4 + 1 = B(-2)(1) \\Rightarrow -2 = -2B \\Rightarrow B = 1\\)",
              "\\(x = -2\\): \\(4 - 8 + 1 = C(-3)(-1) \\Rightarrow -3 = 3C \\Rightarrow C = -1\\)",
              "\\(x = 0\\) par check: bayan \\(\\frac{1}{(-1)(1)(2)} = -\\frac{1}{2}\\); dayan \\(-1 + 1 - \\frac{1}{2} = -\\frac{1}{2}\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 4x + 1}{(x - 1)(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\dfrac{1}{x - 1} + \\dfrac{1}{x + 1} - \\dfrac{1}{x + 2}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "6 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 3x + 4}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 3x + 4}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Barabar degrees (2 = 2): fraction improper hai, is liye pehle taqseem.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "Do not forget the quotient 1 in front."
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\((x + 1)(x + 2) = x^{2} + 3x + 2\\)",
              "\\(x^{2} + 3x + 4 = 1(x^{2} + 3x + 2) + 2\\): quotient 1, baqi 2",
              "\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 3x + 4}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = 1 + \\dfrac{2}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\)",
              "\\(2 = A(x + 2) + B(x + 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = -1\\): \\(A = 2\\); \\(x = -2\\): \\(2 = -B \\Rightarrow B = -2\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} + 3x + 4}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = 1 + \\dfrac{2}{x + 1} - \\dfrac{2}{x + 2}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "7 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + 5x + 1}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\) into partial fractions and check at \\(x = 0\\). (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + 5x + 1}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein aur \\(x = 0\\) par check karein.)",
            "explanation": "Improper (2 = 2): taqseem karein, phir baqi wala fraction Case I se todein.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "Only the proper part is resolved."
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(2(x^{2} + 3x + 2) = 2x^{2} + 6x + 4\\); \\((2x^{2} + 5x + 1) - (2x^{2} + 6x + 4) = -x - 3\\)",
              "\\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + 5x + 1}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = 2 + \\dfrac{-x - 3}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}\\)",
              "\\(-x - 3 = A(x + 2) + B(x + 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = -1\\): \\(-2 = A\\); \\(x = -2\\): \\(-1 = -B \\Rightarrow B = 1\\)",
              "\\(x = 0\\) par check: bayan \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\); dayan \\(2 - 2 + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + 5x + 1}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = 2 - \\dfrac{2}{x + 1} + \\dfrac{1}{x + 2}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "8 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{x^{3} + x^{2} + 1}{x^{2} - 1}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{x^{3} + x^{2} + 1}{x^{2} - 1}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Improper (3 > 2): pehle taqseem, phir denominator ke factors bana kar Case I.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "Step 1: Multiply out the denominator"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(x(x^{2} - 1) = x^{3} - x\\); tafreeq: \\(x^{2} + x + 1\\)",
              "\\(1(x^{2} - 1)\\); tafreeq: baqi \\(x + 2\\); quotient \\(x + 1\\)",
              "\\(\\dfrac{x^{3} + x^{2} + 1}{x^{2} - 1} = x + 1 + \\dfrac{x + 2}{(x - 1)(x + 1)}\\)",
              "\\(x + 2 = A(x + 1) + B(x - 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = 1\\): \\(3 = 2A \\Rightarrow A = \\dfrac{3}{2}\\); \\(x = -1\\): \\(1 = -2B \\Rightarrow B = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{x^{3} + x^{2} + 1}{x^{2} - 1} = x + 1 + \\dfrac{3}{2(x - 1)} - \\dfrac{1}{2(x + 1)}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "9 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{x^{2} - x + 2}{x(x - 1)^{2}}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} - x + 2}{x(x - 1)^{2}}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper (2 < 3); \\(x\\) ghair-mukarrar aur \\(x - 1\\) do baar mukarrar hai (Case II).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "one constant for \\(x - 1\\), and one for each power of"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} - x + 2}{x(x - 1)^{2}} = \\dfrac{A}{x} + \\dfrac{B}{x - 1} + \\dfrac{C}{(x - 1)^{2}}\\)",
              "\\(x^{2} - x + 2 = A(x - 1)^{2} + Bx(x - 1) + Cx\\)",
              "\\(x = 0\\): \\(2 = A\\)",
              "\\(x = 1\\): \\(2 = C\\)",
              "\\(x^{2}\\) ka coefficient: \\(1 = A + B \\Rightarrow B = -1\\)",
              "Check, \\(x\\) ka coefficient: \\(-2A - B + C = -4 + 1 + 2 = -1\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{x^{2} - x + 2}{x(x - 1)^{2}} = \\dfrac{2}{x} - \\dfrac{1}{x - 1} + \\dfrac{2}{(x - 1)^{2}}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "10 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + x + 3}{(x + 1)^{3}}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + x + 3}{(x + 1)^{3}}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper (2 < 3); \\(x + 1\\) teen baar mukarrar hai (Case II, \\(n = 3\\)).",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "no other value of \\(x\\) switches off \\(A\\) or \\(B\\) alone"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + x + 3}{(x + 1)^{3}} = \\dfrac{A}{x + 1} + \\dfrac{B}{(x + 1)^{2}} + \\dfrac{C}{(x + 1)^{3}}\\)",
              "\\(2x^{2} + x + 3 = A(x + 1)^{2} + B(x + 1) + C = Ax^{2} + (2A + B)x + (A + B + C)\\)",
              "\\(x = -1\\): \\(2 - 1 + 3 = C \\Rightarrow C = 4\\)",
              "\\(x^{2}\\): \\(A = 2\\); \\(x\\): \\(1 = 2A + B \\Rightarrow B = -3\\)",
              "Check, constant: \\(A + B + C = 2 - 3 + 4 = 3\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{2x^{2} + x + 3}{(x + 1)^{3}} = \\dfrac{2}{x + 1} - \\dfrac{3}{(x + 1)^{2}} + \\dfrac{4}{(x + 1)^{3}}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "11 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{x + 3}{(x + 1)^{2}(x - 1)}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{x + 3}{(x + 1)^{2}(x - 1)}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper (1 < 3); \\(x - 1\\) ghair-mukarrar, \\(x + 1\\) do baar mukarrar.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "Why: every other term contains \\(x - 1\\)."
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(\\dfrac{x + 3}{(x + 1)^{2}(x - 1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x - 1} + \\dfrac{B}{x + 1} + \\dfrac{C}{(x + 1)^{2}}\\)",
              "\\(x + 3 = A(x + 1)^{2} + B(x + 1)(x - 1) + C(x - 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = 1\\): \\(4 = 4A \\Rightarrow A = 1\\)",
              "\\(x = -1\\): \\(2 = -2C \\Rightarrow C = -1\\)",
              "\\(x^{2}\\) ka coefficient: \\(0 = A + B \\Rightarrow B = -1\\)",
              "Check, constant: \\(A - B - C = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{x + 3}{(x + 1)^{2}(x - 1)} = \\dfrac{1}{x - 1} - \\dfrac{1}{x + 1} - \\dfrac{1}{(x + 1)^{2}}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "12 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{3x^{2} + x + 4}{(x^{2} + x + 1)(x + 1)}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{3x^{2} + x + 4}{(x^{2} + x + 1)(x + 1)}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper (2 < 3); \\(x^{2} + x + 1\\) irreducible hai (\\(1 - 4 = -3 < 0\\)): Case III aur aik linear factor.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "makes \\((Ax+B)(x+3)\\) zero, whatever \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(\\dfrac{3x^{2} + x + 4}{(x^{2} + x + 1)(x + 1)} = \\dfrac{Ax + B}{x^{2} + x + 1} + \\dfrac{C}{x + 1}\\)",
              "\\(3x^{2} + x + 4 = (Ax + B)(x + 1) + C(x^{2} + x + 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = -1\\): \\(3 - 1 + 4 = C(1 - 1 + 1) \\Rightarrow C = 6\\)",
              "Phailayein: \\((A + C)x^{2} + (A + B + C)x + (B + C)\\)",
              "\\(x^{2}\\): \\(3 = A + 6 \\Rightarrow A = -3\\); constant: \\(4 = B + 6 \\Rightarrow B = -2\\)",
              "Check, \\(x\\): \\(A + B + C = -3 - 2 + 6 = 1\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{3x^{2} + x + 4}{(x^{2} + x + 1)(x + 1)} = \\dfrac{6}{x + 1} - \\dfrac{3x + 2}{x^{2} + x + 1}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "13 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{6x^{2} + x + 3}{(2x - 1)(x^{2} + 1)}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{6x^{2} + x + 3}{(2x - 1)(x^{2} + 1)}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper (2 < 3); \\(2x - 1\\) linear aur \\(x^{2} + 1\\) irreducible hai.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "\\(x^{2} + 1\\) is irreducible (\\(b^{2} - 4ac = -4 < 0\\))"
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(\\dfrac{6x^{2} + x + 3}{(2x - 1)(x^{2} + 1)} = \\dfrac{A}{2x - 1} + \\dfrac{Bx + C}{x^{2} + 1}\\)",
              "\\(6x^{2} + x + 3 = A(x^{2} + 1) + (Bx + C)(2x - 1)\\)",
              "\\(x = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\): \\(\\dfrac{6}{4} + \\dfrac{1}{2} + 3 = A\\left(\\dfrac{1}{4} + 1\\right) \\Rightarrow 5 = \\dfrac{5}{4}A \\Rightarrow A = 4\\)",
              "\\(x^{2}\\): \\(6 = A + 2B \\Rightarrow B = 1\\)",
              "constant: \\(3 = A - C \\Rightarrow C = 1\\)",
              "Check, \\(x\\): \\(-B + 2C = -1 + 2 = 1\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{6x^{2} + x + 3}{(2x - 1)(x^{2} + 1)} = \\dfrac{4}{2x - 1} + \\dfrac{x + 1}{x^{2} + 1}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "14 Factorize \\(x^{4} + x^{2} + 1\\) and resolve \\(\\dfrac{2x}{x^{4} + x^{2} + 1}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(x^{4} + x^{2} + 1\\) ke factors banayein aur \\(\\dfrac{2x}{x^{4} + x^{2} + 1}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Factors ke liye perfect square banayein, phir do irreducible quadratics ke liye Case III.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "Why: the book states the factors directly."
            },
            "steps": [
              "\\(x^{4} + x^{2} + 1 = (x^{4} + 2x^{2} + 1) - x^{2} = (x^{2} + 1)^{2} - x^{2} = (x^{2} + x + 1)(x^{2} - x + 1)\\)",
              "Dono quadratics ka \\(b^{2} - 4ac = 1 - 4 = -3 < 0\\): irreducible",
              "\\(2x = (Ax + B)(x^{2} - x + 1) + (Cx + D)(x^{2} + x + 1)\\)",
              "\\(x^{3}\\): \\(A + C = 0\\); \\(x^{2}\\): \\(-A + B + C + D = 0\\); \\(x\\): \\(A - B + C + D = 2\\); constant: \\(B + D = 0\\)",
              "\\(C = -A\\), \\(D = -B\\): \\(x^{2}\\) se \\(-2A = 0 \\Rightarrow A = 0, C = 0\\); \\(x\\) se \\(-2B = 2 \\Rightarrow B = -1, D = 1\\)"
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(\\dfrac{2x}{x^{4} + x^{2} + 1} = \\dfrac{1}{x^{2} - x + 1} - \\dfrac{1}{x^{2} + x + 1}\\)"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "15 Resolve \\(\\dfrac{x^{3} + 3x + 1}{(x^{2} + 1)^{2}}\\) into partial fractions. (5 marks)\n(\\(\\dfrac{x^{3} + 3x + 1}{(x^{2} + 1)^{2}}\\) ko partial fractions mein todein.)",
            "explanation": "Proper (3 < 4); \\(x^{2} + 1\\) irreducible aur do baar mukarrar: Case IV.",
            "book_ref": {
              "topic_id": "8b8c688b-1f4e-5e96-bbf4-28dacde02c2c",
              "quote": "a linear numerator \\(Ax + B\\) over each quadratic power"
